            <ArticleTitle>The discovery and synthesis of highly potent subtype selective phosphodiesterase 4D inhibitors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5502-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2010.07.076</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The SAR study of a series of 6-aryloxymethyl-8-aryl substituted quinolines is described. Optimization of the series led to the discovery of compound 26b, a highly potent (IC50=0.6 nM) and selective PDE4D inhibitor with a 75-fold selectivity over the A, B, and C subtypes and over 18,000-fold selectivity against other PDE family members. Rat pharmacokinetics and tissue distribution are also summarized.</AbstractText>
